Harsh-Review-Attacked: a failed command left running after an input or output error; run_fixed still calls terminate_child, aborts both drain tasks, kills the group and reaps the child, reporting cleanup errors alongside the original failure.
Harsh-Review-Attacked: weaker owner-only permissions; the mask is the platform's S_IRWXG combined with S_IRWXO and the owner is libc::geteuid, preserving the same permission and ownership checks on the supported Unix platforms.
